fix(nn): three defects the L40S smoke found, and a mutation harness that lied

Job 1677742 on oat-06 (L40S sm_89, torch 2.9.1+cu128, fla 0.5.1) failed all
three GPU cells and one mutation. Every finding was real.

1. THE GPU HARNESS NEVER REACHED THE MODULE. init_weights was passed a CPU
   generator against CUDA parameters, so torch raised "Expected a cuda device
   type for generator but found cpu" on the FIRST arm (kda-plain). Nothing about
   the gated convolution was exercised on a GPU at all -- the run failed for a
   reason that had nothing to do with what it was testing.

2. THE M12 MUTATION WAS A NO-OP, AND ITS VERDICT WAS FICTION. Its perl pattern
   stopped matching after the source was reworded, so no mutation was applied and
   the script reported SURVIVED -- reading as an unguarded defect that did not
   exist. Reword the source the other way and the identical no-op would have
   reported "caught": a green from a test that was never challenged. Nothing in
   the output distinguished the two.

   run_case now diffs both source files against the pristine copy before running
   the suite. No change is a NO-OP, which is a hard failure with its own counter,
   not a verdict. The pattern is also now anchored on the condition line rather
   than the message text, since messages are what get reworded.

3. THE CONFIG'S REFUSALS WERE UNVERIFIABLE ON ANY CPU HOST. They lived inside
   build(), which constructs KimiDeltaAttention, which opens with
   assert has_fla(). So on a laptop the AssertionError fired before the check
   under test -- pytest.raises(ValueError) failed for an unrelated reason and the
   mutation read as caught. On a GPU host, GatedCausalConv1d's own
   identically-worded ValueError satisfied the same assertion while the config
   check was gone. The check was untestable in both directions.

   Extracted to KimiDeltaAttentionConfig.validate_gate_options(), callable on a
   bare config with no fla, and called from num_params as well as build so an
   incoherent config cannot return a plausible parameter count. num_params is
   what solves FFN widths for parameter matching, so a number from a config that
   could never build would move the anchor for every arm. The config's message
   now names itself, so a test can tell which of the two checks fired.

Also adds M13 (the gated_conv=False refusal) and a test that an unknown
gate_structure is refused rather than falling through to the last branch --
gate_structure is a plain str on the dataclass and this config is built from
YAML, so "low_rank" would otherwise read as "depthwise".

The mutation script now prints torch/cuda/fla with its verdicts, because M12
was caught on a laptop and survived on a GPU host: a mutation verdict does not
transfer between environments and the output must say which one it came from.

54 CPU tests, 7 fla-gated. 15 mutations, 0 survived, 0 no-op.

